Phase 6 — Demonstrate Load Balancing

Verify that NGINX distributes requests across the three application containers.
The NGINX configuration adds an X-Upstream response header.
This header identifies the upstream address selected for the request.
Generate multiple requests

for i in $(seq 1 9); do

  curl -sI http://localhost:8080/ | grep -i X-Upstream

done

Expected behavior:
The upstream container addresses should rotate across the three application instances while they are healthy.

Inspect logs
docker compose logs         --tail=100 nginx app1 app2 app3
Follow logs in real time:    docker compose logs -f

Important observation
The Application is identical regardless of which instance serves it.

